{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact IDR-1 head b801b1a9dff1065e634ef04024ee7b9d3a8ec8bf on builder/idr1-identifier-docs-20261113, all 4 artifacts, for request 567ef991 under promise 53426ce1 and review request b0f00eac. The reader pages state the cutover's identifiers correctly, with one exception. One sentence of `docs/scopes.md` states what the `genesis-conflict` incident names, and the source contradicts it.\n\nRequired change: the `genesis-conflict` sentence in `docs/scopes.md`, section \"Identity and genesis\".\n\n- The page says: \"The operator incident `genesis-conflict` names both entries.\" The sentence before it names two applied results, so a reader takes \"both entries\" to mean those two results.\n- `incidentsOf` (`packages/scope/src/operator.ts:91`) names the entry that ran the clause `conflict` and the creator's entry that sent the creation request (`input.message.of.from.seq`). It does not name the earlier applied result. The comment at `operator.ts:84-86` says the same.\n- State the two entries that the row names.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `docs/scopes.md`, against source at the head. `SequenceRef` is `{ scope, genesis }`. `GenesisInput` holds the seed, a `GenesisNonce` and the source (`packages/contract/src/entry.ts:35`), and each later entry carries `genesis` (`entry.ts:31`). `DOMAINS` holds nine tags, among them `artroom-input-1` (`packages/contract/src/intent.ts:12-22`). `isGenesisNonce` and `genesisInputDigest` come from `@generalbusiness/dap-bytes` (`domains.ts:59`, `66`, exported by `index.ts`).\n- Every other changed line in `docs`, `docs/manual`, the four package READMEs and the identifiers note. Each replaces \"incarnation\" with the scope ID and genesis, or with the genesis nonce, and I found no other statement that the source contradicts.\n- The split of `notes/implementation/cd-dropped-kind-checks.md`. I compared each section of the note at 57e893c0 with the four files at the head. \"Plain seals\", \"Named-owner seals\", \"Entry points whose admission or refusal changed\" and \"Other test changes\" are unchanged in their new files. The fault table rows are unchanged. The kind table rows are unchanged.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 57e893c0 is an ancestor. Four commits change 23 paths, all Markdown, all under the 4 artifacts.\n- Cheap checks. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. `check-doc-links` checks 1,245 local links and finds 0 broken. The commit-message check passes: 4 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean.\n- Tests. No test reads a changed file. Two test files name a changed path, and only in comments: `failed-claims-close-register.defect.scope.test.ts:360` and `destination.test.ts:177`. The head needs no gate.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The pages name one identity: a scope ID and the hash of its genesis entry. They name the kind as a fact of the seed.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The pages change no code, and the refusal names they give (`wrong-genesis`, `genesis-conflict`) match the source.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note for the planner: the request says that three groups of sections move unchanged. That holds. The head also rewrites the prose that stays in the main note. It merges sentences, adds semicolons, and turns the quotation of ruling e7787de0 item 5 into a paraphrase. It merges the `platform:destination@5` and `@6` rows into one row with the same digests. I read each rewritten sentence and found no change of fact. The request does not mention these edits.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:778bb7edb33c55c174ce25c545971893a7a44b46","binding":"assigned","head":"b801b1a9dff1065e634ef04024ee7b9d3a8ec8bf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2ec5f56961081ab6f9282b7f7982b68db2e5c329\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:53426ce1a034047e1dde1f672ec6f1edb85b4c4b\"]","review_fron